From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: put only the clocks that were got

When of_clk_get() fails at index i, the error path puts all num_clks
clocks. Slot i holds an error pointer, so clk_put() warns. This
happens on every deferred probe. Put only the first i clocks, and
report the error with dev_err_probe().

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c	2026-10-23 06:49:01.399271474 +0000
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c	2026-10-23 06:49:01.411271587 +0000
@@ -872,11 +872,12 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < pd->num_clks; i++) {
 		pd->clks[i].clk = of_clk_get(node, i);
 		if (IS_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk)) {
-			error = PTR_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk);
-			dev_err(pmu->dev,
-				"%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d: %d\n",
-				node, i, error);
-			goto err_put_clocks;
+			error = dev_err_probe(pmu->dev, PTR_ERR(pd->clks[i].clk),
+					      "%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d\n",
+					      node, i);
+			/* put only the clocks we got, not the error pointer */
+			clk_bulk_put(i, pd->clks);
+			return error;
 		}
 	}
 
